12. SOURCE ARTIFACT
The source artifact is the preserved representation of the regulatory material used to create the computational rule set.
It may contain:
PDF
HTML
XML
JSON
structured publication
authority data
machine-readable standard
The source artifact shall be stored through the OneDraft object-storage subsystem where legally and technically permissible.
The database retains the provenance metadata.

13. SOURCE HASHING
Every imported source artifact should receive a cryptographic content hash.
Conceptually:
source_content
      ↓
SHA-256
      ↓
content_hash
The hash provides an integrity identifier for the regulatory source used by the engine.

