}
Example:
INPUT:
building.height

OPERATOR:
<=

THRESHOLD:
45

UNIT:
m

RESULT:
PASS / FAIL

17. APPLICABILITY ENGINE
A rule must first be determined to be applicable.
The engine therefore performs:
RULE
 ↓
APPLICABILITY TEST
 ↓
APPLICABLE / NOT APPLICABLE / UNDETERMINED
The engine must not report a rule violation merely because a rule exists.
It must first establish that the rule applies to the project.

18. APPLICABILITY INPUTS
Applicability may depend upon:
jurisdiction
building type
occupancy
construction type
building area
building height
number of storeys
site conditions
project scope
alteration type
new construction
existing building status
fire classification
occupant load
accessibility classification
energy classification
project date
These values are derived from the Project Model and project metadata.

19. APPLICABILITY STATES
Initial applicability states:
APPLICABLE
NOT_APPLICABLE
UNDETERMINED
CONDITIONAL
SUPERSEDED
EXEMPT
UNDETERMINED is a valid state and must not automatically become PASS.

20. COMPLIANCE DETERMINATION STATES
Validation results shall support:
PASS
FAIL
WARNING
REVIEW_REQUIRED
NOT_APPLICABLE
UNDETERMINED
ERROR
The distinction between FAIL and REVIEW_REQUIRED is critical.
A rule that cannot be deterministically evaluated must not be represented as a failed rule unless the applicable logic establishes failure.

21. SEVERITY MODEL
Initial severity levels:
INFO
LOW
MEDIUM
HIGH
CRITICAL
Severity is independent from result status.
For example:
status = REVIEW_REQUIRED
severity = HIGH
is valid.

