58. DETERMINISTIC EXECUTION
Given identical:
model_version
code_manifest
engine_version
rule_set
the Compliance Engine should produce the same result.
This is a core reproducibility requirement.

59. COMPLIANCE ENGINE VERSION
Every compliance run records:
engine_version
rule_set_version
This permits historical comparison between engine releases.
A change in computational logic must not silently rewrite historical results.

60. RULE VERSIONING
Rules may change over time.
The system therefore treats rule definitions as versioned objects.
Conceptually:
RULE 100
VERSION 1
VERSION 2
VERSION 3
Each rule version is associated with its source version.

61. RULE HASH
Each normalized rule definition should receive a content hash.
Conceptually:
normalized_rule
      ↓
SHA-256
      ↓
rule_hash
This provides deterministic identification of the rule logic used.

62. APPLICABILITY HASH
A resolved applicability set should also be hashable.
Conceptually:
project characteristics
+
jurisdiction
+
code manifest
+
rule versions
      ↓
applicability hash
This supports reproducibility and cache validation.

63. COMPLIANCE CACHE
Safe deterministic compliance results may be cached using:
project_id
model_version_id
code_manifest_id
engine_version
rule_set_version
If any component changes, the cache becomes invalid.

64. STALE RESULT PROTECTION
A compliance result generated for:
MODEL VERSION 17
must not be presented as current for:
MODEL VERSION 18
